B.f3w=new A.y("Frame","Twelve vertebrae that each hold a pair of ribs.")
B.eXV=new A.y("Frame","Five big, strong vertebrae that carry most of your upper body's weight.")
B.eYC=new A.y("Frame","The sacrum and coccyx. The tailbone is what is left of a tail from our far-off ancestors.")
B.eSb=new A.y("Frame","You have 12 pairs of ribs. They make a cage that protects your heart and lungs and moves when you breathe.")
B.f86=new A.y("Frame","The sternum is a flat bone in the middle of your chest that holds your ribs together at the front.")
B.eT1=new A.y("Frame","The most often broken bone, and the only long bone that lies sideways.")
B.eMk=new A.y("Frame","Two flat triangle bones on your back that let your arms swing in a big circle.")
B.eVA=new A.y("Frame",'The humerus. The bump at its end is the "funny bone": really a nerve that gets squashed.')
B.eMf=new A.y("Frame","Two bones, the radius and ulna, that twist round each other when you turn your hand over.")
B.eQQ=new A.y("Frame","Eight small wrist bones plus the long bones of your palm and fingers: 27 in all.")
B.eVF=new A.y("Frame","The hip bones carry your body's weight and protect organs in your tummy.")
B.eTa=new A.y("Frame","The femur is the longest and strongest bone in your body, about a quarter of your height.")
B.f3T=new A.y("Frame","A small bone that shields your knee joint, like a built-in knee pad.")
B.eUv=new A.y("Frame","The tibia carries most of your weight below the knee. The thin fibula next to it helps hold the ankle steady.")
B.faE=new A.y("Frame","Seven ankle bones and long toe bones. Your big toe is important for balance.")
